  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1032 PM CDT FRI AUG 14 2026\n\nThe main story over the next several days will be our prolonged\nand dangerous heat wave. A strengthening upper level ridge will\nlead to increasing temperatures over the weekend and into next\nweek. Temperatures will soar into the mid to upper 90s for most\nof the region through Monday. Those across our western areas will\nsee readings around 100-101 degrees at times. Continued humid\nconditions will keep heat indices generally in the 105-109 range.\nA few locations may briefly see heat indices in the 110-112 range\nover the weekend. Similar to our thinking last night, the areal\ncoverage will likely not be widespread enough to warrant an\nupgrade to an Excessive Heat Warning at this time. We will\ncontinue to monitor the trends and upgrade if necessary. Heat\nAdvisories are currently in effect through Sunday evening.\n\nThis pattern will continue to promote a typically summertime\nconvection regime with low to moderate (20-50%) chances for\nshowers and storms. Greatest chances for showers and storms will\nbe across our southern areas as deeper moisture spreads inland.\nThose across central and north-central Alabama will likely remain\ndry as ridging helps keep a lid on things. However, an isolated\nshower or storm wouldn't be surprising across north-central\nAlabama.\n\n95/Castillo",
